<article class="env-lemma" id="0FXV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FXV">Lemma <span data-tag="0FXV">36.22.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ and $g : Y \to S$ be morphisms of schemes. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X$ and $Y$ are tor independent over $S$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every affine opens $U \subset X$, $V \subset Y$, $W \subset S$ with $f(U) \subset W$ and $g(V) \subset W$ the rings $\mathcal{O}_ X(U)$ and $\mathcal{O}_ Y(V)$ are tor independent over $\mathcal{O}_ S(W)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there exists an affine open overing $S = \bigcup W_ i$ and for each $i$ affine open coverings $f^{-1}(W_ i) = \bigcup U_{ij}$ and $g^{-1}(W_ i) = \bigcup V_{ik}$ such that the rings $\mathcal{O}_ X(U_{ij})$ and $\mathcal{O}_ Y(V_{ik})$ are tor independent over $\mathcal{O}_ S(W_ i)$ for all $i, j, k$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: use More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/08HX" data-tag="08HX">15.62.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>